flowchart TB
    ORCH["CallOrchestrator<br/><b>does not know or care which one ran</b>"]:::orch
    ORCH --> SEAM{{"IntakeStrategy - the seam (D10)"}}:::seam

    SEAM --> S1["<b>PASSIVE</b> - P3, the one we build first<br/>'เล่าปัญหาได้เลยค่ะ'<br/>customer talks, we listen and transcribe.<br/>No AI in the loop with the customer."]:::now
    SEAM --> S2["<b>GUIDED</b> - P8<br/>TTS asks for the missing slots:<br/>'โรงพยาบาลไหนคะ' 'วันที่เท่าไหร่คะ'<br/>still one-way, but it fills gaps"]:::later
    SEAM --> S3["<b>CONVERSATIONAL</b> - P8<br/>a real AI caller that talks WITH them<br/>while they wait"]:::later

    S1 --> OUT
    S2 --> OUT
    S3 --> OUT
    OUT[("<b>same output contract, always</b><br/>IntakeResult: turns + slots + recording_ref<br/>+ finalize_reason + is_partial")]:::out

    OUT --> DOWN["everything downstream is unchanged.<br/>Brief, matching, workstation, storage:<br/>none of them can tell which strategy ran."]:::down

    NOTE["<b>why the seam exists.</b> The user asked for pre-call<br/>intake to be modular so it can BECOME a full AI caller<br/>later without a rewrite. Getting the output contract<br/>right now is what makes that a swap instead of a rebuild."]:::note

